JUCE X11: keep a fixed-size window's min/max size hints across setBounds().

Applied by tools/build-podman.sh -setup-host to a clean export of the pinned JUCE commit when
building the AudioPluginHost used by -debug-linux. The JUCE submodule is never modified.

XWindowSystem::setBounds() calls updateConstraints(), which sets PMinSize|PMaxSize for a
non-resizable window, then immediately rewrites WM_NORMAL_HINTS with only USSize|USPosition.
XSetWMNormalHints replaces the whole property, so the limits never survive: GNOME treats every
fixed-size JUCE window as maximisable, and a maximised plugin window stretches the editor.
Verified on JUCE 8.0.12 (submodule 501c0767) by sending _NET_WM_STATE maximise to the
loudness editor window: 1244x1004 -> 3840x2096 before this patch.

--- a/modules/juce_gui_basics/native/juce_XWindowSystem_linux.cpp
+++ b/modules/juce_gui_basics/native/juce_XWindowSystem_linux.cpp
@@ -1781,6 +1781,20 @@
             hints->y      = newBounds.getY();
             hints->width  = newBounds.getWidth();
             hints->height = newBounds.getHeight();
+
+            // updateConstraints() above has just published PMinSize|PMaxSize for a fixed-size
+            // window, but XSetWMNormalHints replaces the WHOLE property -- so without this the
+            // limits are wiped on every setBounds and the window manager sees every
+            // non-resizable window as resizable. GNOME then maximises it on Super+Up, a
+            // top-edge drag or a title double-click, and a fixed-size plugin editor ends up
+            // stretched across the whole screen. Carry the limits into this write too.
+            if ((peer->getStyleFlags() & ComponentPeer::windowIsResizable) == 0)
+            {
+                hints->min_width  = hints->max_width  = newBounds.getWidth();
+                hints->min_height = hints->max_height = newBounds.getHeight();
+                hints->flags |= PMinSize | PMaxSize;
+            }
+
             X11Symbols::getInstance()->xSetWMNormalHints (display, windowH, hints.get());
         }
 
